Q: Checkmarx: Second-Order SQL Injection attack in c# A: <p>Doing this satisfied CheckMarx:</p>

<pre><code>public OdbcDataReader ExecuteQuery(string sql)
{
    var cmd = new OdbcCommand(sql.Replace("'", ""), connection);
    return cmd.ExecuteReader();
}
</code></pre>

<p>Interestingly, I scanned the method on its own, and using a command did not satisfy it:     </p>

<pre><code>public OdbcDataReader ExecuteQuery(string sql)
    {
        OdbcCommand cmd = connection.CreateCommand();
        cmd.CommandText = sql;
        return cmd.ExecuteReader();
    }
</code></pre>

Q: How to accumulate data from iterated queries as a subarray of a parent row using CodeIgniter A: <p>I don't think your $query variable there is actually an array, but rather a result set.  You ought to put that into an array as well.  Maybe something like this:</p>

<pre><code>$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('questions');
$result_array = array();
$i = 0;
foreach($query-&gt;result_array() as $row){
    $result_array[$i] = $row;
    $result_array[$i]['answers'] = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get_where('answers', array('question_id'=&gt;$row['question_id']), 4);
    $i++;
}

var_dump($result_array);
</code></pre>

Q: How to mock JPA repository&#39;s find method in unit tests A: <p>If i remember well your test have to use this :</p>

<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>    @Before
    public void init() {
        MockitoAnnotations.initMocks(this);
    }
</code></pre>
